id: pm-vcs-390t
title: "Phase 4: pm-vcs versions its own source"
description: "The package must track its own source code in pm-vcs alongside git, so the claim that pm-vcs is a working version control system is demonstrated by the repository itself rather than asserted in a README. The self-hosted history ships as a bundle in the repository and a CI gate proves the bundle's tip tree is exactly the source tree, so source cannot change without the pm-vcs history following it."
type: Epic
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:28:24.621Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-04T11:15:37.978Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: A tracked bundle holds pm-vcs history of pm-vcs's own source; a CI gate fails when the bundle's tip tree differs from the git-tracked source in any byte; the gate re-verifies every object against its own id; the check is deterministic and cannot pass by regenerating the bundle from a dirty tree
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-vcs-tr2a,parent,"2026-07-31T06:28:27.158Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-04T05:48:33.087Z",pi-agent,"Design: a committed text bundle (selfhost.bundle) holds pm-vcs history of the git-tracked source. accept:self-host is verify-only: it reads the committed bundle and the committed source both from HEAD (git cat-file / git archive), so a dirty working tree cannot affect the verdict and regenerating the bundle without committing it changes nothing. self-host:write is the only path that writes the bundle. The exclusion set is data in self-host.json; the gate builds its source tree from git ls-files minus exclusions, so a tracked file in neither the bundle nor the exclusion set fails closed. Trees use the legacy (FileId-free) v1 encoding via engine buildTree so the bundle is deterministic — tree ids depend only on content+mode. parseBundle re-hashes every object against its own id (point 3); importBundleObjects stores them. Byte-exactness = root tree id equality, which covers content and mode."
  "2026-08-04T06:46:50.532Z",pi-agent,"Implemented scripts/self-host.ts with --write/--check separation, self-host.json data file, selfhost.bundle committed artifact, test/self-host.test.ts (15 real tests), wired accept:self-host into package.json release:check and CI, documented in ARCHITECTURE.md section 10. Verified coverage 100/100/100 with the locked pm-cli 2026.8.1 (a stale local node_modules at 2026.8.3 had silently changed the test harness and dropped the pmClient fallback branch from coverage; npm ci restored the locked version)."
  "2026-08-04T10:36:08.158Z","harness:claude-code","Review round on PR 10 addressed. Five reviewer findings fixed: git ls-files read NUL-delimited so a newline in a path cannot desynchronise the gate's own path list; readSourceFiles now raises the absent-path failure its docstring already promised, which also removed an unreachable missing-path diagnostic in main that could never fire; extractHead materializes HEAD through a detached git worktree instead of git archive piped to tar, removing the only non-git binary the gate depended on and which the Windows job never exercised despite accept:self-host sitting inside release:check and prepublishOnly; spawnSync launch failures are distinguished from non-zero exits so a missing git cannot read as a clean verdict; and loadConfig, non-commit ref tips and object omission all gained real tests. One finding was rejected as a false positive: Sourcery called import.meta.dirname non-standard, but it landed in Node 20.11 and this package declares engines node >=22.18.0 with a green 22 and 26 matrix. CodeRabbit accepted that rebuttal. A sixth defect surfaced from the review rather than in it: the gate did not prove the bundle is SELF-CONTAINED. verifySelfHost resolves the tip through a store the source side has already written every blob into, so a bundle omitting an object it declares still resolved by borrowing the missing bytes from the source, and parseBundle accepts a header listing an object the body omits — meaning a truncated bundle was reported byte-identical. The declared object list is now compared against the lines actually carried, the only check in the function that consults no store. Verified the whole loop end to end: committed the source, watched the gate fail exit 1 naming both changed files and both tree ids, regenerated the bundle, watched it pass."
  "2026-08-04T11:15:37.977Z",pi-agent,"Addressed the coverage round: added scripts/self-host.ts to coverageGate.sources, fixed the NODE_V8_COVERAGE lcov corruption by overriding it to /dev/null in test helpers, exported the script's private functions and main for testability, wrote 18 new tests bringing scripts/self-host.ts to a genuine 100/100/100 (25 source files reported, up from 24). Decided scripts/audit-git-identities.ts is out of scope for 100/100/100: its uncovered branches are defensive error paths in streamGit (timeout, spawn failure, stdin error) that cannot be triggered without mocking, plus the untestable entry-point guard."
tests[1]{command,scope}:
  "npm run accept:self-host",project
body: ""
